# BIMtrieval configuration.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` in the repository root and fill in your own values:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is git-ignored and is never printed, logged, or baked into a container
# image. Three applications read it independently — ingestion and the backend
# each resolve these names themselves; neither imports the other's code.

# --- Ingestion / write connection -------------------------------------------
# The account that CREATES and POPULATES the BIM schema: tables, migrations,
# imported entities, relationships, and stored vectors. It needs CREATE on the
# database, plus CREATE EXTENSION for pgvector and (only for
# `bim-db-init --with-readonly-role`) CREATEROLE.
#
# This is the ONLY connection that ever writes BIM data.
db_url=postgresql://bim_rag:CHANGE_ME@localhost:5432/bim_rag

# --- Backend / read-only connection -----------------------------------------
# The dedicated read-only role the query backend connects through, so the API
# structurally cannot modify the model corpus even if a query were malformed.
# Create it with:
#
#     python -m bim_rag.db_admin.bootstrap_readonly_role
#
# which generates a password, grants SELECT only, and writes this line for you —
# without ever printing the credential.
#
# Optional: if unset, the backend falls back to `db_url` above. That works, but
# it gives up the read-only guarantee, so set it for anything but a scratch run.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://bim_rag_query_ro:CHANGE_ME@localhost:5432/bim_rag

# --- Docker Compose only (optional) --------------------------------------
# The container stack runs its OWN PostgreSQL in a volume; it does not use
# db_url/DATABASE_URL above, which point at your host database. These override
# the local-only defaults baked into compose.yaml. The production overlay
# (compose.prod.yaml) REQUIRES all four rather than defaulting them.
#
# POSTGRES_USER=bimtrieval
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# POSTGRES_DB=bimtrieval
# POSTGRES_RO_PASSWORD=      # the backend's dedicated read-only role

# --- OpenAI ------------------------------------------------------------------
# YOUR key. BIMtrieval never ships one, never proxies one, and never asks for a
# key in the browser — the frontend talks only to your local backend, and only
# the backend calls OpenAI.
#
# Without it the app still starts and remains inspectable: the 3D viewer, model
# catalog, and floor plans work, and question answering reports that no key is
# configured rather than fabricating an answer.
#
# Get one at https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-your-own-key-here
